  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Amol Suresh Shetty vs State Of Maharashtra on 6 August, 2025 2025:Bhc-As:33579 7- Ba 3 Tikam In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Criminal Appellate Jurisdiction Bail Application No.3078 Of 2025 Amol Suresh Shetty ... Applicant Vaishali V/s. Anil Tikam The State of Maharashtra ... Respondent Digitally signed by Vaishali Anil Tikam Date: 2025.08.06 Mr. Aniket Nikam a/w. Advocate Abhilasha Pawar i/b. 21:24:20 +0530 Advocate Amit Icham for the Applicant. Mr. A.A. Palkar, App , for the State. Coram : Ashwin D. Bhobe, J. Dated : 6th August, 2025 P.C.:",
    "facts": "2. By the present application filed under Section 483 of Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023, Applicant is seeking bail in connection with C. R. No.50 of 2025 registered with Karkamb Police Station, Solapur, for the offences punishable under Sections 123, 274, 275, 3(5), of B. N. S. and under Section 3(1) (a), 3(1)(zz)(v), 26(1), 26(2)(1), 26(2)(v), 27(1) punishable under Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. 3. Mr. A. Nikam, states that the said crime is registered as Sessions Case No.48 of 2025 and is pending before the Additional Sessions Judge, Pandharpur. 4. There are 10 Accused in the crime. Applicant is Accused No.7. 5. Aforesaid crime was registered at the instance of Mr. Umesh Subhash Bhuse, working as Assistant Commissioner in the Office of Food and Drugs Administration. Case of the prosecution is that information about preparation of adulterated milk in a tin shed at village Bhose, Taluka Pandharpur, was shared with the informant. Accordingly, a raid was effected with the assistance of the police, wherein, some of the Accused persons were found in the premises raided. Investigation, revealed Applicant's involvement in the crime, as a supplier of whole milk powder \"Nandini\". 6. Applicant was arrested on 11.04.2025. Since, then, the Applicant is in jail. Bail Application at Exh. 4 Sessions Case No.48 of 2025 filed by the Applicant was rejected by the Additional Sessions Judge Pandharpur by the order dated 01.07.2025.",
    "arguments": "7. Mr. A. Nikam, learned Advocate for the Applicant submits that the Applicant is not involved in the Crime No.50 of 2025. He submits that the allegations against the Applicant is of having supplied whole milk powder \"Nandini\" to the Accused No.1 and 2. He submits that neither any material in support of the said allegation is produced on record nor any recoveries made from the Applicant. He submits that the Applicant has been implicated in the present crime, without any basis and/ or without any supporting material. He submits that the Applicant has no criminal antecedents. 8. Mr. Amit Palkar, learned APP for the State submits that the 7- BA 3078 of 2025.doc involvement of the Applicant in the present crime is of a supplier who is said to have supplied whole milk powder \"Nandini\" to Accused No.1 and 2. She submits that apart from the said allegation, there is no other allegations against the Applicant. She submits that no recoveries are made from the Applicant.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "7. Mr. A. Nikam, learned Advocate for the Applicant submits that the Applicant is not involved in the Crime No.50 of 2025. He submits that the allegations against the Applicant is of having supplied whole milk powder \"Nandini\" to the Accused No.1 and 2. He submits that neither any material in support of the said allegation is produced on record nor any recoveries made from the Applicant. He submits that the Applicant has been implicated in the present crime, without any basis and/ or without any supporting material. He submits that the Applicant has no criminal antecedents.",
    "respondent_arguments": "8. Mr. Amit Palkar, learned APP for the State submits that the 7- BA 3078 of 2025.doc involvement of the Applicant in the present crime is of a supplier who is said to have supplied whole milk powder \"Nandini\" to Accused No.1 and 2. She submits that apart from the said allegation, there is no other allegations against the Applicant. She submits that no recoveries are made from the Applicant.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
